# Keep the build context to sources. docker/ is needed, but the build stage copies it separately.
.git
.github
.claude
.superpowers
docs
# The docs site, with the build output and caches Hugo and its tests leave in it. docs-site.yml builds it.
site
**/target
**/gwt-unitCache
**/.settings
**/.project
**/.classpath
**/*.bak
# IDE and OS files: the build-stage COPY would see them change and re-run Maven.
**/.idea
**/*.iml
**/.vscode
**/.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
compose*.yaml
# What the Install manual's Backup and Restore writes beside compose.yaml: the backup's two files (and the .sql of a
# backup taken before the move from MariaDB), restic's settings, with their keys, and the folder restic restores into.
# A backup lying in the checkout would otherwise go to the builder and into a layer, and run Maven again.
/logicaldoc-db.*
/logicaldoc-files.tgz
/restic.env
/backup
# The demo stack's sources and files: the overlay mounts them, and the image doesn't need them
docker/demo
# The desktop clients no module builds, so a change to one doesn't re-run Maven. clients/office/ stays: healdan-api
# packages the Office add-in into its jar.
clients/helper
clients/libreoffice
clients/icons
**/node_modules
